course: dictionary
lesson: 6250
title: Capital letters and one word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have a capital letter and some do not, and the capital letter tells you something. «The Mohawk people lived in what is now New York State.» Mohawk has a capital M because it names a people, just as Seneca and Oneida are names with capitals.
explain: The same spelling can also mean something else. «Ben asked for a mohawk haircut, with the sides shaved and a strip of hair standing up.» Here mohawk is a small-letter word for a hairstyle. The sentence tells you what it means, so you can check the clues around it.
explain: Read the whole sentence before you decide. Ask: is this a person, a language, or a haircut? In «the Mohawk language», the word language is a big clue that Mohawk names a way of speaking.
fact: A capital letter often shows a name, such as a person, place or people.
fact: «Mohawk» with a capital letter means the Mohawk people or their language.
fact: «Mohawk» with a small letter means a hairstyle, with the sides shaved and a strip of hair standing up.
fact: In the UK, a mohawk is often called a «mohican».
fact: The Haudenosaunee Confederacy was a league of peace, and the Mohawk were one of its nations.
exercise: «The Mohawk people lived in what is now New York State.» Why does Mohawk have a capital letter? | Because it is a hairstyle | Because it is a long word | *Because it is the name of a people | Because it starts a new sentence
exercise: «Ben got a mohawk haircut.» What is a mohawk here? | A tall building in New York | *A hairstyle with shaved sides and a strip of hair standing up | A language spoken in Quebec | A people of North America
exercise: In the UK, what else is a mohawk often called? | Moped | *Mohican | Mohawk Park | Mohair
test: «The Haudenosaunee Confederacy united the Mohawk, Oneida, Onondaga, Cayuga and Seneca.» What was the Haudenosaunee Confederacy? | A language spoken only in Ontario | A hairstyle worn in New York | A river in Quebec | *A league of nations that worked together for peace
test: Which sentence uses mohawk to mean a hairstyle? | "She speaks the Mohawk language at home." | "The Mohawk are a First Nations people." | *"Dan's new mohawk stood up tall." | "The Mohawk lived in New York State."
exam: Which spelling is correct when mohawk names the people or their language? | MOHAWK | Mo hawk | *Mohawk | mohawk
